===== Installation =====

Get the ''brcm47xx'' firmware image ''openwrt-15.05-brcm47xx-mips74k-linksys-wrt320n-v1-squashfs.bin'' from https://downloads.openwrt.org/chaos_calmer/15.05/brcm47xx/mips74k/

Upgrade that via factory firmware's Administration -> Firmware Upgrade selection.

==== Custom image Installation past v22.03.7 ====

  * **Note 1:** In any case, be sure to start with the installation instruction, as mentioned at the top of this page. After that procedure, you should be able to use sysupgrade to the latest OpenWRT v22.03.7.
  * **Note 2:** Set a static IP on the device and make sure you can connect to it. Resetting the device configuration will result in no IP, after which you should theoretically be able to set a static IP from recovery mode: [[:docs:guide-user:troubleshooting:failsafe_and_factory_reset]]

Due to limited ram and flash (32/8), OpenWRT isn't officially supported anymore on this device. Therefore it is wise limit the amount of packages in a custom image.

=== Make sure your system is up to date ===
<code>
sudo apt-get update && sudo apt-get upgrade
sudo apt-get install build-essential libncurses-dev zlib1g-dev gawk git sudo apt install build-essential libncurses-dev zlib1g-dev gawk git gettext libssl-dev xsltproc rsync wget unzip python3 python3-distutils
</code>
=== Setting up the environment ===
<code>
mkdir ~/openwrt && cd ~/openwrt
VERSION="23.05.5"
wget https://downloads.openwrt.org/releases/$VERSION/targets/bcm47xx/mips74k/openwrt-imagebuilder-$VERSION-bcm47xx-mips74k.Linux-x86_64.tar.xz
tar -J -x -f openwrt-imagebuilder-*.tar.xz
cd openwrt-imagebuilder-*/
</code>
=== Always be sure to have a clean working environment, by resetting the environment to zero ===
<code>
make clean
</code>

